bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    seed_jit_explicit_f64_option_some_typed_readers_lose_low_mantissa_bits_2026-11-27, 0, "Repro (seeds aa542919a298e130 base and f391cc81a8b1f257, aarch64, JIT; interpreter correct): val c: f64? = Some(0.1); print c ?? 9.0, if val v = c: print v, print c.unwrap() all print 0.09999999999999998 on the JIT (interpreter 0.1); == 0.1 is false for ??, if val, unwrap, a fn mk() -> f64?: return Some(0.1) result, and [f64?] element ?? (probe f4: JIT false false true false false false, interp all true). Only the typed match Some(v) arm reads it exactly. The explicit Some payload holds raw IEEE bits while these readers decode a tagged float and drop the low 3 mantissa bits. Found while fixing seed_jit_erased_f64_option_some_binds_raw_bits_2026-11-27. Design call for the coordinator: storing an explicit Some(x) at an f64? slot in the raw f64? form (tagged float) would likely fix this and subsume that bug's per-call boundary conversion."
    seed_jit_explicit_f64_option_some_typed_readers_lose_low_mantissa_bits_2026-11-27, 1, "2026-11-27 f64opt-inline fix (work/f64-option-inline-repr-20261127): root cause = a typed float optional reaches readers in three forms: Option enum (rt_enum_new) holding RAW IEEE bits (explicit typed Some(x)), Option enum holding a tagged heap float (generic/untyped producers: [f64].at, fn pick<T> -> T?, untyped fn w(x): Some(x)), and the flat tagged float (return x into f64?). Readers lowered to rt_unwrap_or_self + UnboxFloat, which decodes raw bits as a legacy inline TAG_FLOAT (payload << 3) and drops the low 3 mantissa bits. Fix: new dual-lane rt_option_float_bits (Rust value/objects.rs + C runtime_native.c, registered in runtime_sffi.rs, runtime_symbols.rs, elf_utils.rs, runtime.h) returns the exact bits in one enum lookup (raw payload, or a registered HeapFloat's value, or as_float of the flat word); mir lowering_core.rs read_present_float_option_payload = that call + lossless F64 self-cast (+ F64->F32 for f32?); lowering_expr_builtin.rs rt_unwrap_or_self float arm uses it; hir stmt_lowering typed match Some(v) arm over a float optional routes through the same reader (fixes [f64].at matched on base). Residuals: raw bits that alias a live registered HeapFloat address; the double whose bits equal the nil word (3, a denormal) still takes the ?? default because lower_coalesce keeps its Some(nil) payload test (an untyped Some(nil) in an f64? slot is the identical word; dropping the test regressed w(nil) ?? 9.0 to a denormal, so it was kept) -- needs a tag separate from the payload; f64?.unwrap() on None does not trap on the JIT (pre-existing, base reads a denormal, fix 0.0; interpreter errors)."
    seed_jit_explicit_f64_option_some_typed_readers_lose_low_mantissa_bits_2026-11-27, 2, "Evidence (aarch64, base seed e2479b4127a0a3a9, fix seed e157f5dcf31f5692): compiler/tests/seed_jit_f64_option_exact_payload.rs base red on 0.1, denormal bits 2, 1e-300 (mask 15415) and f32 (2) -> 8/8 green, incl. bit-exact spl_f64_to_bits/spl_bits_to_f64 readers over a quiet NaN with payload 0x7ff8000000000005, a negative NaN, and denormals with bits 1, 2, 9 (base 39 per value), plus boxed producers ([f64].at, pick<T>, untyped Some) that a raw-bits-only reader misread; native_project native_typed_f64_option_some_readers_keep_exact_bits_against_c_runtime (archive linked against the core-C runtime, so the C twin runs) mismatch=63999 -> 0; test/01_unit/language/f64_option_some_exact_payload_spec.spl (in-development; JIT + interpreter; readers + NaN-bits fixtures) base 1/3 -> 3/3; Rust-seed native-build (SIMPLE_NATIVE_BUILD_RUST=1) of the reader matrix and the NaN-bits probe green except the residuals below. Expression match, if val Some(v) = c and statement match over [f64].at / pick<T> / explicit Some all 0.1 (base: denormal for at / pick). Perf (alternated, taskset -c 12, user-time min / median): 4e7 Some+??+unwrap 14.33 / 14.67 s -> 13.87 / 14.32 s (n=4), RSS 1.94 GB both; struct-of-f64? 2e8 field ?? reads 13.70 / 15.78 s -> 13.29 / 15.90 s (n=10), load 14-25. Not fixed here: inline no-allocation representation (seed_typed_f64_option_some_heap_allocates_per_some_never_released_2026-11-27), generic Bi<f64> match (subject erased to any; peer residual of seed_jit_erased_f64_option_some_binds_raw_bits_2026-11-27), print sink (seed_jit_f64_option_some_print_sink_reads_raw_payload_as_value_2026-11-27), dict f64 literal (seed_jit_dict_f64_literal_value_read_loses_low_mantissa_bits_2026-11-27). LLVM backend not run. Pure-Simple compiler (src/compiler/50.mir switch_operators_calls.spl bitcast_float_enum_payload) keeps one enum-handle form with bitcast payload; read, not run."

